# Git branch and PR workflow

- Never commit or push straight to `main`/`master` for project work.
- Create a descriptive feature branch from up-to-date `main` before implementation commits.
- Push the feature branch with `-u`, then open a PR with `gh pr create`.
- Return the PR URL when done. Merge only when the user asks.
- If work was accidentally committed on `main` locally and not yet pushed, move it onto a feature branch before opening the PR (no force-push to `main`).
